.TH SDL_COMPILE_TIME_ASSERT 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_COMPILE_TIME_ASSERT \- A compile-time assertion.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_COMPILE_TIME_ASSERT(name, x) FailToCompileIf_x_IsFalse(x)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This can check constant values _known to the compiler at build time_ for correctness, and end the compile with the error if they fail\[char46]
.PP
Often times these are used to verify basic truths, like the size of a datatype is what is expected:

.IP
.EX
SDL_COMPILE_TIME_ASSERT(uint32_size, sizeof(Uint32) == 4);
.EE
.PP

The
.BR name
parameter must be a valid C symbol, and must be unique across all compile-time asserts in the same compilation unit (one run of the compiler), or the build might fail with cryptic errors on some targets\[char46] This is used with a C language trick that works on older compilers that don\(aqt support better assertion techniques\[char46]
.PP
If you need an assertion that operates at runtime, on variable data, you should try
.BR SDL_assert
instead\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I name
a unique identifier for this assertion\[char46]
.TP
.I x
the value to test\[char46] Must be a boolean value\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
This macro doesn\(aqt generate any code to run\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_assert (3)
